        "text": "Salmon",
        "text_sha256": "31377fd10d4613f5800e9bb05b06d3d99c5a4be955d05371589fcf620ae25575",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000053",
        "block_index": 53,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Strawberries",
        "text_sha256": "387fe3ba020da494f6b919b38f5af6690effc79ed9108c9dee7956db9e269281",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000054",
        "block_index": 54,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Whole grain bread",
        "text_sha256": "0d0e1427f92f1c8ab7e68f4b285e242cfbb4fa774743774ccfb03861e245ecb1",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000055",
        "block_index": 55,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Yogurt",
        "text_sha256": "bd4c1d9ac7fa95852ad1581dfb4d499f43022d4a71a2f3d1b86eec66c82d8d07",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000056",
        "block_index": 56,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When to talk to your child’s doctor about picky eating",
        "text_sha256": "4401e69dba250955ddaa701a8b795e24763208246c387710214ab01ee5fe4a04",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000057",
        "block_index": 57,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "As long as your toddler is getting enough calories — and isn’t subsisting on cheese puffs — food ruts aren’t harmful to his long-term health. Remember, too, that as a parent, it's your responsibility to serve healthy food to your child — but it's up to him to decide just how much he wants to eat.",
        "text_sha256": "943be05ae7730362bd0572bf91a57c1add0c7364a4784ebf7212859daeabe967",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000058",
        "block_index": 58,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Children’s appetites slow down in toddlerhood compared to when they were babies. If, however, you notice that your child isn’t gaining any weight or seems weak, lethargic or unusually irritable, talk to your pediatrician, who can help make sure that your little one is getting all the nutrients he needs.",
        "text_sha256": "2eaa4cefc8cbbab985cd56707ebdb5d2842cdc1bc13f60fe7255007a4b2ff70e",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000059",
        "block_index": 59,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In all likelihood, however, his finicky tastes are just a phase. Hang in there — he should eventually outgrow it.",
        "text_sha256": "31cf35f1088286cff769a5c68957557d38b3779cd81e1493ebbc4827b2a2e284",
        "word_count": 20
      }
    ],
